            <ArticleTitle>Use of Surgimap Spine in sagittal plane analysis, osteotomy planning, and correction calculation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>163-72</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.nec.2012.12.007</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1042-3680(12)00146-5</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Over the past 3 decades the sagittal plane has received increasing attention from the scientific community and spine surgeons alike. There remains a lack of clear and concise methods for incorporating surgical techniques and radiographic parameters to achieve the best possible outcome on a patient-specific level. This article proposes a new method for a treatment approach to sagittal malalignment by incorporating new digital tools for surgical planning. This technique offers a consistent approach to adult spinal deformity with sagittal-plane components, and can permit optimization in consistently achieving proper postoperative spinopelvic alignment.</AbstractText>
